# Momentum repository rules

Implementation update (2026-10-28): immutable task/step IDs, Hive schema-v3 step migration, and exact positive-minute handling are now implemented. The AI tools and focus-session feature remain planned. See [verified foundation changes](docs/details.md#j-implemented-foundations).

Read [details.md](docs/details.md) for source evidence, [PRD.md](docs/PRD.md) for scope,
[design.md](docs/design.md) for implementation contracts, [architecture.md](docs/architecture.md)
for boundaries, and [phases.md](docs/phases.md) for execution order. Plans are not implemented features.

## Highest-priority code rule: reuse before writing

- Search the relevant source with rg before adding code. Prefer standard-library and
  installed-package capabilities; do not rebuild trusted library functionality.
- Make the smallest safe, readable change. Avoid duplicate parsers, wrappers,
  speculative interfaces, oversized functions, and unrelated refactors.
- Apply SOLID, DRY, KISS, and YAGNI pragmatically. Dependency injection is useful for
  clock/storage/HTTP tests, not a reason to introduce a framework.
- Existing reuse points include HiveService, showTaskFormDialog,
  showQuickAddTaskDialog, task_time_utils.dart, text_formatters.dart,
  LogRewardPolicy, and the reusable widgets under lib/widgets/.

## Repository and architecture

- Inspect current code and git status before editing. Preserve pre-existing changes.
- This is a Flutter/Dart client with an optional Python FastAPI/MongoDB starter;
  it is not a Python web application requiring a replacement frontend.
- Keep snake_case file names, existing lib/models, services, screens, widgets,
  utils, constants folders, and the small backend layout.
- Widgets use HiveService and Hive listeners. Keep persistence/business rules out
  of new widget code. Keep API serialization in ApiClient and socket lifecycle in
  SyncService. Avoid circular imports and new global service dependencies.
- Preserve current task, routine, journal, instruction, reward, theme, profile,
  streak, and productivity behavior unless the requirement explicitly changes it.
- Default task storage is local. AI assistance may be enabled independently;
  MOMENTUM_CLOUD_SYNC_ENABLED remains false for the AI pilot. Never
  interpret X-User-Id, a local profile, or the WebSocket user_id as authentication.
- REST persists cloud changes; WebSockets signal changes. Clients never access
  MongoDB directly. Do not add separate Windows/mobile codebases or microservices.

## Persistence and compatibility

- tasksBox is Box<List>; date keys and reserved metadata keys share the box.
  Filter metadata from task iteration. Never clear user storage to fix a migration.
- Preserve Task adapter typeId 0 and Hive fields 0-18, plus TaskStep typeId 1
  and fields 0-8. Fields 0-15 remain the original Task format. Append fields
  with compatible defaults and migration tests. Regenerate task_model.g.dart using
  build_runner only for an authorized model change; review generated defaults.
- Existing descriptions contain phase and schedule metadata. Preserve their
  compatibility until an explicit, tested migration replaces that representation.
- Do not change reward formulas or recurring-series identity incidentally while
  fixing task identity. See docs/design.md for the distinction.

## Dependencies and protected content

- Inspect pubspec.yaml, pubspec.lock, and backend/requirements.txt first. Explain
  any new dependency's concrete benefit; avoid unrelated upgrades.
- Do not add Django, SQLAlchemy, PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka, Kubernetes, or another
  state-management package merely because they are familiar.
- Motor retirement is a separate backend maintenance task, not a local MVP dependency.
- Do not modify secrets, private keys, real data, .git internals, generated platform
  files, or build caches unless the authorized task specifically requires it.
- Never run activate.ps1 or clean_up.ps1 as a routine test: they stop processes,
  delete artifacts, and activate.ps1 runs flutter create .
- A documentation-only request authorizes documentation, not source implementation.

## Testing and security

- Add/update meaningful tests for changed behavior, including failure, legacy-data,
  duplicate-title, restart, and date-boundary cases when relevant.
- Use temporary Hive directories and an isolated MongoDB test database. Do not
  point api_test.ps1 at personal data; it performs writes and starts a server.
- Run relevant tests and report actual commands/results. run.ps1 treats Flutter
  test failure as a warning; its exit status alone is not a release gate.
- Never claim a build, test, sync flow, or platform works without executing it.
- Validate external payloads; do not silently substitute today's date for corrupt
  remote data. Never log task bodies, journal text, credentials, or MongoDB URIs.
- Use verified identity and owner filters before public sync. Secrets do not belong
  in --dart-define values, source files, or documentation.

## Workflow

1. Read the requirement and relevant source; identify confirmed versus assumed facts.
2. Search for reusable code; choose the smallest compatible implementation.
3. Implement only authorized changes, preserving unrelated working-tree content.
4. Run appropriate tests and inspect the diff; report environmental blockers honestly.
5. Consult docs/ for project analysis and plans when needed. Keep README.md at
   the repository root and other project Markdown documentation in docs/.
   Update the six planning documents in docs/ when behavior, architecture, or configuration
   changes. Keep feature IDs, scope, file mappings, estimates, and verification aligned.
6. Report changed files, results, limitations, and the next concrete action.

## AI feature extension

- User constraint: Goblin Tools is feature inspiration only. Never integrate its
  API, private endpoints, scraping, embedded pages, code, assets or branding.
  Implement Momentum's own UI, prompts, logic and storage. A separately selected
  model running locally on the device is allowed. The user now requires no external
  inference API dependency. See docs/OFFLINE_VOICE.md; earlier hosted-provider
  plans are historical and must not override this constraint.
- For the current offline voice work, reuse VoiceCapture, VoiceTaskParser and
  VoiceTaskService. Bundle models at build time; never add a hosted fallback.
- Future PRD A1-A7/AX designs must respect the offline constraint and typed operation
  contracts. Do not build seven independent backends or autonomous agents.
- Do not add provider keys or external inference calls to the offline workflow.
  Optional legacy task sync remains a separate, disabled-by-default feature.
- AI output is a draft. Only an explicit user action may apply it to tasks or text.
  Never auto-complete tasks, award rewards, send replies, or execute generated code.
- Preserve raw estimates separately from actual focus time and reward accounting.
  Duration normalization now preserves every positive integer; only legacy
  null/zero default to 15. Validate AI estimates explicitly before constructing
  TaskStep; do not use the legacy default to conceal invalid model output.
- Use stable step IDs for reordering, completion and focus checkpoints. Do not
  expand pipe-delimited descriptions into the new structured-step database.
- Default to selected context only and no AI history. Test empty/invalid output,
  timeouts, stale previews, duplicate Apply, and timer restart/background behavior.
